course: dictionary
lesson: 12871
title: Strong feeling words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words show how strongly someone feels. Enraptured is one of the strongest. It means filled with great joy, so happy that you forget everything else around you. «The audience sat enraptured while the violinist played.» Nobody is whispering or checking the time; they are completely caught up in the music.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Ask: what does the person stop doing, or forget? «Mole was enraptured by the river on his first day.» Mole did not think about home or the time; the water held all his attention. Now swap in a weaker word, such as pleased, and see whether the sentence still shows how caught up he was. It shows much less.
explain: Enraptured is a step above pleased or delighted. Those words show happiness, but enraptured means carried away by something beautiful. A good check is to ask whether the person would forget everything else. If they would, enraptured fits.
fact: Enraptured means filled with great delight and joy, so happy that you forget everything else.
fact: It can also mean completely charmed or fascinated by something beautiful.
fact: The verb is enrapture: enraptures, enraptured and enrapturing are all forms of it.
fact: Enraptured is stronger than pleased or delighted.
fact: «Enraptured» often shows up when someone stops, stares or listens without moving.
exercise: «The children were enraptured by the puppet show.» What does enraptured mean? | Hungry for lunch | Slightly annoyed | Bored and tired | *Completely delighted and caught up
exercise: «Ava was enraptured by the painting, and she did not hear her name being called.» What does the clue «did not hear her name» show? | *She was completely absorbed in the painting | She was angry with the painting | She was lost and looking for a map | She had already left the gallery
exercise: Tom says enraptured means just a bit happy. What is the right meaning? | Just a little bit happy | Very cold and wet | Bored and sleepy | *Filled with great joy, so caught up you forget everything else
test: «The crowd was enraptured as the acrobat walked across the high wire.» What does enraptured mean here? | Cross about the noise | *Completely caught up in wonder and delight | Nervous and wanting to leave | Sleepy after a long day
test: The music ___ the crowd. Which word fits the gap? | *enraptures | endures | enrages | enters
exam: Which sentence shows the strongest feeling? | «Sam was tired after school.» | «Sam was pleased with his drawing.» | *«Sam was enraptured by the stars, and he forgot the time.» | «Sam was a little glad.»
